    "title": "Firefighters respond to reported house fire in Montgomery County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By WHIO Staff ,\n48 minutes ago Stock photo of a fire engine racing to the scene of an emergency. A Texas skydive instructor and student were critically injured Saturday, Feb. 19, 2022, after their parachutes failed to open during a tandem jump. By Matthew Gush Firefighters responded to reports of a house fire in Montgomery County late Wednesday night.\n[DOWNLOAD: Free WHIO-TV News app for alerts as news breaks ]\nThe fire was reported in the area of Bricker Avenue and West Third Street around 10:45 p.m., a Montgomery County dispatch supervisor confirmed.\nTRENDING STORIES:\nThe supervisor couldn’t provide additional information.\nEmergency scanner traffic indicates that the flames have been extinguished.\nNews Center 7 is working to learn more and will continue to follow this story.\n[SIGN UP: WHIO-TV Daily Headlines Newsletter ]",
